#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096699 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096499 :question/id #uuid "29a0265e-ad88-5ac9-88fe-878aa4f0d0bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-531" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$$\nf'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0) = 2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C \\\\ 2 & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2cdeff7-1bd1-52cc-b4d2-58765a1e715e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = - (1)/(2(x - 1)) + \\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094094} {:answer/id #uuid "e264582e-6aa3-5da8-b05d-657aca25a556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{x - 1} + \\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094095} {:answer/id #uuid "43d2def0-e7d1-54fb-834f-84b6876ea10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{x - 1} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094096} {:answer/id #uuid "518e0850-647a-5199-8686-13cfd746ca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{x - 1}" :db/id #