$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ecc69b-755b-5462-8126-6d18390bc9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251113} {:answer/id #uuid "51d0ffb6-6f64-5896-abdf-17cb6f16197d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251222} {:answer/id #uuid "b403e123-9b40-51a1-b551-d4ee97aeac63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252131} {:answer/id #uuid "bcae2f92-0655-5e91-b689-f83acfb52de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252218} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6281fe-2594-5ca0-8ac1-0635fb6762ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ecc69b-755b-5462-8126-6d18390bc9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251113} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e18fea8-a6e5-5302-8876-2d446746feb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252970}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dd37419-0acf-5e07-951f-998d06a1d1c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-119045" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0877a493-110b-5bc5-b8f0-b95a212d57cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250624} {:answer/id #uuid "404b89d5-fb90-54b3-9fd1-b0ed48ad3aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251087} {:answer/id #uuid "7d24a901-b539-53de-9ab1-410020de269d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}+2x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251597} {:answer/id #uuid "b2cb0cc0-4925-5d83-a3b2-07b01eb84c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+3x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252117} {:answer/id #uuid "c233f23d-d374-5888-ae7d-c2e80f985c8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0877a493-110b-5bc5-b8f0-b95a212d57cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250624} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb5f0d15-ef01-5c2b-8b45-e12411c1710b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70e058ec-5742-5754-884d-951409c47fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-119046" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)-4x=1$ that satisfies the condition $f(1)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(1)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =2(1)^{2}+1+C \\\\ -1 & =2+1+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "063d885c-e465-53c3-8fc9-1185c7d2a24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}-2{e}^{-2x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250604} {:answer/id #uuid "2352b722-ccc2-5fb7-b992-99d02c98a38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{x}^{2}+2{e}^{-2x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250855} {:answer/id #uuid "4927258a-3e5d-57d8-ad17-4093de1cc583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251163} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf4bda2-85a0-506d-86cb-55bb6ebcdb9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251595} {:answer/id #uuid "febdfee4-02c6-55f5-970a-792e4ad18364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "febdfee4-02c6-55f5-970a-792e4ad18364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252790} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a412b91-1bde-571f-aacb-eb83ca3e461a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252937}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea7f0932-1ce6-52df-a5dc-f1855b5f815e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119075" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}+{e}^{-2x}=8x$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8x-{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8x-{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})+C \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =4(0)^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2(0)}}{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4861751d-591d-55c3-986e-ef2a5b44047f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251157} {:answer/id #uuid "66412d8c-05ca-5d19-b457-71e9ce3cbc83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251394} {:answer/id #uuid "73dd9002-7420-57dd-aa1f-4e2c936b2b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x+{e}^{x/2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251508} {:answer/id #uuid "906cd958-b4d4-5e47-8a8a-6773bb3989db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251780} {:answer/id #uuid "f2723fb9-3ffe-529a-aa32-10cf5b96b2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{x/2}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906cd958-b4d4-5e47-8a8a-6773bb3989db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251780} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2e489f5-5c3c-511b-8803-0c93ae9edf09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5aa7094-d36f-5005-a0c6-3e11c04ef4b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-119083" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-2x={e}^{x/2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+{e}^{x/2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{e}^{x/2})\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & ={0}^{2}+2{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 2 & =0+2(1)+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+2{e}^{x/2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a99c790f-778d-5a5f-97a8-2b99e8f49b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a99c790f-778d-5a5f-97a8-2b99e8f49b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318143} :answer-field/id #uuid "877e6d0c-39d3-53e7-b2ef-a30f289e7b59" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318720}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb49f682-fb8a-5bf1-935c-970f0a98d037" :question/math-academy-id "q-347842" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $8x-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=5.$\n\n$y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,+${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}+8x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+4({2}^{2})+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{8}{3}+16+C \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{40}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203a3079-ee5c-560e-8635-760c7bf1066a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "203a3079-ee5c-560e-8635-760c7bf1066a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319489} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74970cc-7b2d-58bc-b6f8-f2dd0e1d894a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320686}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bd28782-0820-5dae-86e8-4965e6266454" :question/math-academy-id "q-352066" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c11b83c6-f179-56e1-8175-cb7b2c642c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c11b83c6-f179-56e1-8175-cb7b2c642c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{x+1}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319981} :answer-field/id #uuid "320d7bcf-5061-50ea-841d-459ccafe7cbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320280}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c687828d-8060-5328-a166-293d79967235" :question/math-academy-id "q-352068" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x+1}\\,{y}^{′}=4$ that satisfies the condition $y(3)=10.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int (x+1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(2(x+1)^{1/2})+C \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(3)=10$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =8\\sqrt{3+1}+C \\\\ 10 & =8(2)+C \\\\ C & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=8\\sqrt{x+1}-6.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c0bcef-46b2-545e-843c-328afdee9423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c0bcef-46b2-545e-843c-328afdee9423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319845} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fb75ca-ef4f-5f30-adaf-5e38a644e069" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320493}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f433502-a7f8-5681-8b4b-ad43723d3a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-352075" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$f(x)=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+C \\\\ 2 & =3(1)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c2556ab-42eb-5b03-9b82-ffafb8c7bdf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6{x}^{3}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330340} {:answer/id #uuid "340e3d02-facf-523f-89ff-093dd1bcd18f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{x}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330411} {:answer/id #uuid "aae0e4e4-5033-5e88-827b-62d31ab7b6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331464} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f11883-6eaf-55d0-bcf4-0414977256ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332068} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcec268-59b1-5bae-be4e-f748d99e9108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdcec268-59b1-5bae-be4e-f748d99e9108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332183} :answer-field/id #uuid "9815a89d-855b-59fa-9302-62052d559095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332469}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "860439d5-1eb6-58cf-8abd-cc9242b3ec59" :question/math-academy-id "q-50044" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=2$\n \n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=2{x}^{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =2(-1)^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =-2+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{3}+4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8cac35-ec47-5085-bcb0-da00cb39efe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330181} {:answer/id #uuid "2ecb6c15-4ffb-53a5-a6a3-acd959f971df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330360} {:answer/id #uuid "82e52b8f-937b-5b6c-bf07-b2a4477afeb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331109} {:answer/id #uuid "d1cbd642-0604-55df-9d4b-e311b2299017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331810} {:answer/id #uuid "f83e9e7e-87a9-5751-b17a-60d01d2b92ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ecb6c15-4ffb-53a5-a6a3-acd959f971df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330360} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e80a73-b1ef-545c-bc47-759f5717a078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8704e7df-0e87-5dd2-a140-acb85a41ea4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50092" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1.$\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+4x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(1)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{4}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88dad183-ed2b-5a15-83b8-2f429e39030d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331167} {:answer/id #uuid "963a6dbf-bdcb-54b7-b515-ded61ba89b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331284} {:answer/id #uuid "bafaabc4-4fca-516b-a9d6-7ed9697af49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331598} {:answer/id #uuid "fd70074b-45df-5d86-ae50-06ecb0063c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332179} {:answer/id #uuid "ffdab17a-cdb5-59fe-8492-3c8a1b66fd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "963a6dbf-bdcb-54b7-b515-ded61ba89b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331284} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1e6eb7-20e6-5c26-9817-474a9a29bb18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332400}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab41d9c4-5e4f-5845-a572-d7bd4049e427" :question/math-academy-id "q-50159" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-2.$\n\n$$\n(1+2x){f}^{′}(x)-2=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=(1+2x).$ Then $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2\\cdot 0|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351482 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dc989a8-2c75-5f1c-9659-077b9b5ceeed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349599} {:answer/id #uuid "90451e36-0f3c-542c-9624-ec09beef5517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349742} {:answer/id #uuid "96633e09-e5d2-5a83-a534-6acb8fbe9b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349795} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d311c7-63bd-56a8-90ae-daf55b933be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350028} {:answer/id #uuid "eec3251e-786c-5a1a-9eba-fcc26b7bd286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96633e09-e5d2-5a83-a534-6acb8fbe9b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349795} :answer-field/id #uuid "83e5ea7c-8d82-5535-96fc-e39fd184f9e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d35cfdf-da63-5e6d-990c-a2e5c83f1725" :question/math-academy-id "q-8311" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4=0$ given that $y(-1)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-4x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=4$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =-4\\cdot (-1)+C \\\\ 4 & =4+C \\\\ 0 & =C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-4x\\,.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096700 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096494 :question/id #uuid "11c09a26-0e83-5a77-b777-aea8a3594960" :question/math-academy-id "e-5183" :question/problem "Consider the diagram that is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbf{b}=-\\mathbf{c}$\n2. $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$\n3. $\\mathbf{a}=2\\mathbf{e}$\n\n![](images/95/95ae711c1ccbf7543e6d269aa8d817a66e2ac348113ea71f3a1babcbb23d1ca3.png)" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ have different magnitudes. So, $\\mathbf{b} \\neq -\\mathbf{c}$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Statement III is false. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is greater than the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq 2\\mathbf{e}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dee5d942-5b95-5365-b7a4-2d5ac9543f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094922} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b587fd-b686-5435-bb6b-21b51d77a364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094923} {:answer/id #uuid "f85afda0-69ce-5cf3-a723-847227c518d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094924} {:answer/id #uuid "321c235c-8766-57b1-9ff1-c6626b41abe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094925} {:answer/id #uuid "3d788b5a-eb2e-55cd-a75d-8910eaf06ec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094926}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4abd1b-7b83-56eb-8314-223cf698aff6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094921}] :question/id #uuid "9e0c6801-5ef7-5ccd-ab0c-ee92136a4d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-19215" :question/problem "![](images/28/285bc802c51b89c2dd5b64bd3ee5ff41bf49d798110fb0c9f29c59ea00f66cf8.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $b =-2e$\n2. $c =-d$\n3. $b = 2e$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95f37730-b753-5283-add4-6fddb7259ed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095030} {:answer/id #uuid "9682d9f9-ca68-5454-aab8-15febe41b189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095031} {:answer/id #uuid "05b2a283-a165-5811-9676-85ffe8f06528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095032} {:answer/id #uuid "2aab021d-d23b-54cb-a063-e85c7486c5ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095033} {:answer/id #uuid "7202e42e-e2ea-5d4b-96b9-e92f3a811165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095034}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4b2695c0-5527-58d8-a0d1-ea8201ff7061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095029}] :question/id #uuid "5602d163-6088-5c26-9dd7-db2402561aee" :question/math-academy-id "q-20404" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c08ee3645692aa5630bc00d8dcd619fe4e6410b050afb6875339ab0962894ed2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $a =-c$\n2. $c =-\\frac{1}{2}a$\n3. $b = d$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096495 :question/id #uuid "839ed5f5-165f-5de5-aba1-551ac605475f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5212" :question/problem "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](images/f2/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that ![](images/c6/c6714d0a6eaa5c7d354d46e8d6d60da7f3d2011df0fc75773036cf7ae510c5e3.png), find ![](images/24/24878591902884f45f14f5c447bc326586a411a8870b205fc12825a4ab2c738a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite ![](images/5c/5c644b15efcf5a4274de23242a722604ead2ff800ea29ba7a650729227fefdf0.png) in terms of ![](images/27/27f36b1d1846e12e3c50b7d4e47f5745727792d52a48e4d85b689ec36e3d25a0.png) and ![](images/a7/a7b9033c421072576aaf959980d778c319a8ed0f849e08db644b63bc6994088c.png) we can match coefficients to determine the unknown scalar.\n\nTo find ![](images/16/166c90a9c29f99347bff6b397f31d705ec6407a19b4d71246f98308bbd7a5473.png) we want to match the expression\n![](images/fc/fc79367916dd7671c17de4f40b3d83f91d41c2f9988645964de0b53e5b11ab9b.png)\n\nWe are given that one of the components is ![](images/91/91f686c6ca02e85c386cb0f9e80b66beface446d3a541952e0ac91738ad0db37.png) So, we first draw the vector ![](images/d5/d54b9a8919c7b6106fcf5770c62b1823605d7be98a55d5333e73bcfb7528997a.png) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](images/6e/6e1bbbe9eb66856824ff70d16cc2c077519d361546b226a67146e20f15a24dd0.png)\n\n![](images/ea/ea517ac4ca8e0bcf7ba48f23e66f100323d5485f1221219aacfbea9148f4a1af.png)\n\nNote that in ![](images/f1/f1c944e6afa4e9cd84bc68004a2bfd918d81498a727aeb7c56ec627806bf93f6.png), we have:\n\n- ![](images/b7/b7ac390c4e43b2fa2fbb4063632f98869256cea877caa5e5dad4aad33ae94722.png)\n\n- ![](images/7e/7e5f2b01647ab01052fff18ab760273eebe19d47b56051b1953adf587d7f9fb3.png) and ![](images/78/784225d11bf94b7fbd67f8e2395695141eb75b1cb44f89d49b29bb3a2031534b.png) have the same direction\n\nHence, ![](images/21/21261c8ad0d86a9e7300ffc58c57fd76beef9f627492bcfe2051d5e3cfd82a4e.png)\n\nAdditionally,\n![](images/ae/ae9c98ded3aa4317a729571710ad38d973a2d67b5faeb9ad26af7c24ee5c3193.png)\n\nConsequently, ![](images/ae/aee3287ad64a654880216142756811bd4d5232b3dba2f48378b8b1c5241e4316.png)\n\nSince ![](images/46/466863f8c7522ac89896a4233a823be02940535097c28328fa2c9e9e1f4bc3d8.png) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](images/37/3720c5887713d3f7a29be384fe5e883390935b2b9b469af626a8dba968f4da8b.png) we get:\n![](images/4a/4ac145b710c5354b44a4ea1dc820d70f54b5c17985f078fce6313b671ec26fd9.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fbb8f19-f35a-59c4-9b77-8f6c3542ef28" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050467 :topic/math-academy-id 1102 :topic/title "Problem Solving Using Vector Diagrams"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051014 :topic/math-academy-id 1105 :topic/title "Linear Combinations of Vectors and Their Properties"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00092400-4bdb-54aa-b9f7-3bbc79220342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786} {:answer/id #uuid "132972e0-7a7c-5c06-9851-0cd678b28702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284957} {:answer/id #uuid "159ed092-bb37-575a-9d11-ee33122bcff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284980} {:answer/id #uuid "4c63c7e5-c9c3-51e0-9d4a-a4807711e12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285498} {:answer/id #uuid "caceb281-75a2-5c25-ace0-e5023bde2a8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "159ed092-bb37-575a-9d11-ee33122bcff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284980} :answer-field/id #uuid "518cd3fd-d07a-569f-9cb4-9c2cf6e0f0c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287328}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "767cbe5b-8f45-54bf-8422-666ebc7778f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19338" :question/problem "![](images/81/816c4ecbfe49321bc6b2bc0d72eb61d6ddd1aeae7e76a275df0975439dde5865.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/67/6782f2fa59056afd9022edbaf69c44a991bf12a7ac6a190bea3cc08fc7a4996c.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2.5|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.5b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2.5b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2.5b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2.5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cc5590c-f5cf-5e21-9a2e-5e31772b304d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285183} {:answer/id #uuid "35a20bbd-e86d-5f6e-907f-c57e5562aefc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285280} {:answer/id #uuid "531f071e-da47-5a18-876a-8d7ce3863d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285552} {:answer/id #uuid "80ddc038-3db7-5447-8486-3d32260a66f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285973} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a429df-36c3-50d3-a2b3-d9bf1a44b2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a429df-36c3-50d3-a2b3-d9bf1a44b2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286477} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fd9a91d-854c-5377-a157-19bd44fd94f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a4f66a0-1cfd-52d9-be40-ea47c3b77cf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20435" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b7c8c679171c1dcb6ef44b33696ba2ccce87b3f690643af979476d8dfb285ce.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+3b$, find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $3b.$ So, we first draw the vector $3b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/f6/f67af4512a7ab61f862932a60dafc25ef62bc46335b7d7df323fe889f8728e6b.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $3b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =3b+\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+3b=\\frac{1}{2}a+3b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f58b1f0-a1f2-5152-8b50-a3b88cfa03ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253806} {:answer/id #uuid "28d1e0c0-6ce0-5a30-b308-d0185860ae28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254035} {:answer/id #uuid "86b0f05f-4928-50e1-9fee-05c5f1c722c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254862} {:answer/id #uuid "c1aa28fa-00bb-55da-83ba-fd94389b454c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255398} {:answer/id #uuid "f72b66ba-7fc3-5027-b7a4-6cc62030c64e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f58b1f0-a1f2-5152-8b50-a3b88cfa03ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253806} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bffb12d-46cf-5b60-8dd5-5eb835abe4b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "701d4729-670a-58df-8c65-907d28621390" :question/math-academy-id "q-120244" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e595809380e3067934b9f8c86933dd5300fcfb54ce4202eddc0e4196b74cf00.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/0c/0c785e189beebb0a803bceba272db156af6d3b47c690ee9527876f77c65d1891.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0335560b-a354-5aa4-b231-eab70eea8ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253694} {:answer/id #uuid "1e21b15d-d740-5a5b-9c81-a80ec1a76c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253923} {:answer/id #uuid "3400ad14-ce2a-5d97-b3ef-9cad4db20aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254119} {:answer/id #uuid "9588a3fa-37df-5403-bcd0-6fe653faf445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254987} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e8937f-908d-5315-adb1-a5131958d010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3400ad14-ce2a-5d97-b3ef-9cad4db20aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254119} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b1acee-2901-571f-8ea9-fb67bf575d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256132}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :que