+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c8d67718152bc1bc9569213369580b6fc6f5bc1fe0c63b637f14c9f659dfe27.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=\\frac{2}{3}|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{2}{3}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301182} :answer-field/id #uuid "5972d618-ef56-509e-bacd-8caba67f5cfd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5c3e7c8-04d1-5bc5-af15-ec4125ed0196" :question/math-academy-id "q-327046" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3d34b42eb1874894af9675944e97e403d67db92bf96449fd8f87fbb14063a10e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=a+\\lambda b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/c0/c074e514a4ca52868a5c01d7a29182d62493f2cc9